    <title>
        2026.9.11: persist refresh history per note, so an interrupted run re…
    </title>
    <updated>2026-09-11T11:06:25Z</updated>
    <media:thumbnail height="30" width="30" url="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63473642?s=30&amp;v=4"/>
    <author>
      <name>candemircan</name>
      <uri>https://github.com/candemircan</uri>
    </author>
    <content type="html">
      &lt;pre style=&#39;white-space:pre-wrap;width:81ex&#39;&gt;2026.9.11: persist refresh history per note, so an interrupted run resumes

`run` wrote history.json only after the last note, so Ctrl-C discarded the
whole night&amp;#39;s progress: the next run found no history entry and regenerated
every note it had already filled, paying for the LLM and TTS twice. Write the
history after each note instead; notes already refreshed are then skipped on
resume (reps unchanged), and the in-flight note is retried atomically.&lt;/pre&gt;
    </content>
  </entry>
